            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "33a628c9-cad8-4296-9da0-3587eae37fc1",
      "name": "On form submission",
      "webhookId": "ad46d5b2-7d32-4868-ace8-3da8b9111984"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You have access to the user's Equity portfolio, which is in a Google Sheet. You also have access to market data and calculation tools.\n\nThe user has provided this rebalancing instruction:\n{{ $json['How would you like to rabalance your portfolio?'] }}\n\nCRITICAL: Do NOT ask for confirmation or pause. Execute the rebalancing steps immediately.\n\nBEFORE executing the rebalancing, you MUST first ensure all market data is current by following this EXACT sequence:\n\nSTEP 1: Read the portfolio from the sheet to identify all unique tickers (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n\nSTEP 2: Read the MarketStack data sheet to check existing prices for each ticker (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n\nSTEP 3: For EACH ticker, evaluate: (Tool: UpdateMaketStack data)\n   - IF ticker is NOT present in MarketStack sheet → MUST fetch price using MarketDataFetcher\n   - IF ticker IS present → Use existing data, DO NOT fetch\n\nSTEP 4: For EVERY ticker you fetched in STEP 3, you MUST IMMEDIATELY:\n   - Write the ticker symbol, price, and current timestamp to the MarketStack data sheet (Tool: UpdateMaketStack data)\n   - This is MANDATORY — you CANNOT skip this step under any circumstances\n   - Do NOT proceed to rebalancing until this write is confirmed\n\nSTEP 5: Re-read the MarketStack data sheet to VERIFY all tickers now have current data (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n   - IF any ticker still missing or stale → GO BACK to STEP 3\n   - IF all tickers have current data → PROCEED to rebalancing\n\nTo achieve the rebalancing, follow these steps IN ORDER. Do NOT skip any step. Do NOT proceed to the next step until the current step is COMPLETELY FINISHED:\n\nSTEP 1: Read the portfolio from the sheet to get current holdings, quantities, and target allocations (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n   → CONFIRM: You have retrieved all ticker symbols and quantities before proceeding.\n\nSTEP 2: Read the latest market prices from the MarketStack data sheet for EACH ticker in the portfolio (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n   → CRITICAL: CONFIRM: Update the ticker price.\n    - Every ticker has a price. If any ticker is missing a price, STOP and return to the data refresh steps.\n\nSTEP 3: Calculate the current portfolio state including:\n   - Current value of each position (quantity × price)\n   - Total portfolio value\n   - Current allocation % for each ticker\n   - Deviation from target allocation for each ticker (Tool: Calculator)\n   → CONFIRM: All calculations are complete and deviations are known before proceeding.\n\nSTEP 4: Generate rebalancing trades:\n   - Calculate the ideal number of shares needed to reach target allocation\n   - Round to whole shares (NO fractional shares allowed)\n   - Determine BUY, SELL, or HOLD for each ticker (Tool: Calculator with rounding logic)\n   → CONFIRM: Trade list is generated and all share quantities are whole numbers.\n\nSTEP 5: Optimize the trades to ensure:\n   - All trades are executable (no fractional shares)\n   - Total portfolio value remains balanced\n   - Deviations are minimized within the ±2% tolerance (Tool: RebalancingOptimizer)\n   → CONFIRM: Optimized trade list is ready for execution.\n\nSTEP 6: Write the final rebalancing decisions to the Google Sheet (Tool: GoogleSheetsWriter)\n   - Include: ticker, action (BUY/SELL/HOLD), shares, price, total value, new allocation %\n   → CONFIRM: Sheet has been updated successfully.\n\nSTEP 7: VERIFY rebalancing success:\n   - Re-read the portfolio from the sheet (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n   - Re-fetch prices from MarketStack sheet (Tool: GoogleSheetsReader)\n   - Recalculate portfolio state (Tool: Calculator)\n   - Compare actual allocation to target allocation for EACH ticker\n   → CONFIRM: All positions are within ±2% of target.\n\nSTEP 8: If ANY position still deviates by more than ±2% from target:\n   - Go back to STEP 4 and recalculate (Tool: RebalancingOptimizer)\n   - This is attempt #2. If still not within tolerance, try one more time (max 3 total attempts)\n   - If after 3 attempts any position is still outside ±2%, NOTE this in the email/notification but PROCEED to STEP 9\n\nSTEP 9: Send confirmation email (Tool: EmailSender) — The email body MUST include:\n   - Summary of rebalancing action (buy/sell/hold per ticker)\n   - Previous allocation vs new allocation (% and $)\n   - Total portfolio value before and after\n   - Number of shares bought/sold per ticker\n   - Cash remaining/used\n   - Execution timestamp\n   - Deviation from target after rebalancing\n   - Warning if any ticker could not be traded to the ideal target\n   → CONFIRM: Email has been sent.\n\nSTEP 10: Send push notification (Tool: PushNotification) — The notification MUST include:\n   - \"Portfolio rebalanced successfully\" or \"Rebalancing attempted with issues\"\n   - Total portfolio value\n   - Number of trades executed\n   - Largest buy and sell (ticker + $ amount)\n   - Final deviation %\n   - Next review date (7 days from now)\n   - A one-line status like \"All targets within ±2%\" or \"Review required\"\n   → CONFIRM: Notification has been sent.\n\nFINAL CONFIRMATION: Only after ALL 10 steps are complete, respond \"OK\".\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- You CANNOT sell or buy Ticker in fractions\n- Target tolerance: ±2% of total portfolio\n- Maximum 3 rebalancing attempts\n- The MarketStack sheet MUST be updated with fetched prices BEFORE any rebalancing calculation\n- VERIFY the write was successful by reading the sheet again after writing\n- If you skip updating the MarketStack sheet, the rebalancing will FAIL\n\nAlways use tools until complete. Only respond \"OK\" after using all tools when your mission is complete.",
        "options": {
          "maxIterations": 50
        }
      },
